      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As an Avatar creator with 70+ avatars in my world and tons going in and out since January. Allowing people to Favorite your avatars isn't bad at all. I'd recommend adding a watermark to the Avatar icon or maybe even the avatar if you'd like. That way people will visit your world to get the avatar themselves. I go to my world often to see and hear what people are saying/doing. If they want to favorite your avatar that means they like it. If they ever want to switch to your avatar but are already in another world talking they might not bother. If they do want to switch they will drop a portal, walk in, grab what they want, then leave. So your worlds numbers or popularity on the Active chart isn't effected because they aren't staying for more than a minute anyway. My suggestion is to make a world that not only has avatars but is an enjoyable and fun hang out spot as well. Optimize it, bake lighting, have mirrors, props, music, everything toggleable for performance/enjoyment/comfort. This is what will effect your world most. Favoriting is only going to help you as more might switch back and forth to your avatars publicly advertising your world. Also down the road they are adding a Feedback system which will allow people to rate and rank your world. So I suggest focusing on that aspect sooner than later.\n\nYou also aren't considered the way your visitors will see you and your world is they can't favorite your stuff. \"Oh this guy is selfish, wants us to have to waste our time to switch to his work, or ah well I'll just go use my 3 favorite slots on someone more welcoming.\" I don't see people viewing you positively at all.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
